    "helpGuideTitle1": "What is Qur'an Kareem",
    "helpGuideDescription1": "The Holy Quran is the religious text of Islam, believed by Muslims to be the word of God as revealed to Prophet Muhammad through the angel Gabriel. It contains guidance and teachings on various aspects of life, including faith, morality, spirituality, and daily living.",
    "helpGuideTitle2": "How many chapters does the Qur’an Kareem include?",
    "helpGuideDescription2": "114 chapters",
    "helpGuideTitle3": "Can I read separately versicles and chapters?",
    "helpGuideDescription3": "Yes you can. You can jump from one page to another in the way you prefer. You can also mark them so you can directly read them without searching them in the whole book.",
    "helpGuideTitle4": "Can I share the content in other places?",
    "helpGuideDescription4": "Yes you can, أوقات الأذان آزاد الكُردي is an open source app where you are free to use the content.",
    "helpGuideTitle5": "What is the purpose of the app?",
    "helpGuideDescription5": "The main purpose of the app is to offer to the community a native open source mobile app where they can read, listen and save their surahs, ayas or juzs.",
    "helpGuideTitle6": "What are the key features of the app?",
    "helpGuideDescription6": "You can read with no limit the Holy Qur’an, you mark with the bookmarks the last aya you read so you won’t get lost next time you open your Qur’an. You can listen the ayas in case you don’t know how to read it in Arabic and also you can save your most read surahs, ayas or juzs.",
    "helpGuideTitle7": "How can users troubleshoot problems and find solutions? ",
    "helpGuideDescription7": "You can always contact us via email: aabdulrahman1229@gmail.com",
    "helpGuideTitle8": "Are there any known limitations or restrictions in the app?",
    "helpGuideDescription8": "No there is not, you can read and listen as much as you want.",
    "helpGuideTitle9": "Who is the target audience for the app?",
    "helpGuideDescription9": "Everyone who has an interest in getting to know the Holy Qur’an, reading or listen to it. Everyone is welcome.",
